From 74c5ba8b8bc37256e8451d2ef65aad4ef2c52354 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:42:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(app): judge a tap's cutting moves at its thread's core in
 the op verify

A tap on a hole modelled at tap-drill size was still refused after the
program sim learned to sweep its core (#713): the generator's own verify
read the full major diameter against the hole wall and convicted the feed
in and out as gouges. Generate now re-runs the cutting laws with the tap
cut to its ISO 724 basic minor diameter and drops each Gouge the core run
does not also raise. Rapids, shank, holder and fixture verdicts keep the
full diameter; a hole under the minor diameter, a tap over solid metal or
deeper than its hole is still convicted. Builds on austin62jake's
cutting_radius and tap_sim fixtures from #271/#713.

Fixes #266

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
